WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:14.122
distance the village looked beautiful.

2
00:00:15.503 --> 00:00:15.983
But Mrs.

3
00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:19.465
Errol knew that everything was not as lovely as it seemed.

4
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:25.288
On some streets the cottages were in bad shape, and the residents were often sick.

5
00:00:28.676 --> 00:00:29.477
One day Mrs.

6
00:00:29.557 --> 00:00:33.139
Errol happened to meet Reverend Mordaunt on one of the worst streets.

7
00:00:33.159 --> 00:00:36.361
"Look at these cottages," she said.

8
00:00:36.381 --> 00:00:39.223
"Some of them are nearly falling down.

9
00:00:39.243 --> 00:00:43.065
Tenants have told me their roofs are leaking.

10
00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:48.228
And I've seen the damp walls and broken windows when I've visited the sick."

11
00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.830
"It's a shame."

12
00:00:52.011 --> 00:00:53.732
Reverend Mordaunt shook his head.

13
00:00:55.412 --> 00:00:58.193
Mrs. Errol watched some children playing in the dirt.

14
00:00:58.213 --> 00:01:02.815
"I worry about the children who live here.

15
00:01:03.935 --> 00:01:08.096
Meanwhile my son lives in a castle, surrounded by a beautiful park.

16
00:01:09.657 --> 00:01:12.458
He's treated like a prince and can have whatever he'd like."

17
00:01:12.478 --> 00:01:14.939
"You're right.

18
00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:18.320
It's not fair," Reverend Mordaunt agreed.

19
00:01:19.624 --> 00:01:25.868
"Many times I've asked the earl to do something about these cottages, but he doesn't seem to care."

20
00:01:25.888 --> 00:01:31.412
"I wonder Mrs.

21
00:01:31.492 --> 00:01:33.593
Errol tapped her foot as she looked around.

22
00:01:33.613 --> 00:01:37.036
"The earl will do whatever Cedric wants.

23
00:01:38.337 --> 00:01:45.261
If I tell Cedric that these cottages need to be replaced, and he tells the earl—" Reverend Mordaunt

24
00:01:45.481 --> 00:01:49.044
smiled. "Then the cottages will be replaced!"

25
00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:54.642
A few days later, Cedric entered the library.

26
00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:59.445
He didn't greet the earl but went straight to a big chair and sat down.

27
00:02:00.906 --> 00:02:03.747
Lost in thought, he frowned and sighed.

28
00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:09.491
"You look troubled," the earl said.

29
00:02:09.511 --> 00:02:12.272
"Is something bothering you?"

30
00:02:13.753 --> 00:02:15.314
Cedric nodded solemnly.

31
00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:22.142
"When I visited my mother yesterday, she told me about a horrible place in the village.

32
00:02:23.382 --> 00:02:27.685
She cried when she described the cottages where the poor families live.

33
00:02:28.986 --> 00:02:30.787
Their houses are collapsing!"

34
00:02:33.348 --> 00:02:35.989
Cedric got up and leaned against the earl's chair.

35
00:02:36.009 --> 00:02:41.813
"You said that Reverend Mordaunt tells you about the people who live on your land.

36
00:02:42.793 --> 00:02:45.455
But he must have forgotten to mention this place.

37
00:02:46.635 --> 00:02:49.149
If he had, I know you would have helped."

38
00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:53.333
The earl looked uncomfortable as Cedric continued.

39
00:02:53.353 --> 00:02:56.996
"I promised Mama I'd make sure you knew."

40
00:02:58.317 --> 00:03:00.819
Cedric looked up hopefully at his grandfather.

41
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.404
At that moment the earl realized that Cedric was the only person who'd ever trusted him.

42
00:03:08.765 --> 00:03:11.688
Suddenly the earl was ashamed of the miserable cottages.

43
00:03:12.909 --> 00:03:16.552
He was also ashamed to admit that he'd known about them for years.

44
00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.281
"What do you think I should do?"

45
00:03:20.841 --> 00:03:21.942
the earl asked.

46
00:03:21.962 --> 00:03:26.444
"Mama says those cottages must be knocked down and rebuilt.

47
00:03:27.644 --> 00:03:28.865
So that's what you should do."

48
00:03:30.505 --> 00:03:31.966
Cedric's face brightened.

49
00:03:31.986 --> 00:03:34.907
"Let's tell the tenants tomorrow!"

50
00:03:34.927 --> 00:03:38.529
"It may not be tomorrow."

51
00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:41.850
The earl laughed.

52
00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.612
"But the tenants will have new cottages."

53
00:03:48.704 --> 00:03:54.369
When work on the cottages began, Cedric and his grandfather rode to the village almost every day.

54
00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.852
Cedric quickly made friends with the workmen.

55
00:04:00.594 --> 00:04:02.455
One day two men were laying bricks.

56
00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:09.061
"I like learning about new things," Cedric said to the earl.

57
00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:12.884
"Would you mind holding my pony while I talk to these men?"

58
00:04:17.588 --> 00:04:20.771
The earl watched with pride as the men greeted Cedric.

59
00:04:22.552 --> 00:04:27.596
A few minutes later, Cedric returned to tell the earl everything he'd learned about laying bricks.

60
00:04:27.616 --> 00:04:35.142
"He's a good boy," one bricklayer said to the other as they watched Cedric ride away.

61
00:04:35.162 --> 00:04:38.005
"He'll make a fine earl someday."

62
00:04:39.246 --> 00:04:40.587
The second man nodded.

63
00:04:40.607 --> 00:04:43.929
"Lord Fauntleroy is already making a difference.

64
00:04:45.311 --> 00:04:46.852
He has a good effect on the old earl."

65
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.862
That night Cedric sat on the library rug with Dougal.

66
00:04:51.882 --> 00:04:54.763
"Do you remember the night I arrived?"

67
00:04:55.163 --> 00:04:56.364
he asked the earl.

68
00:04:56.384 --> 00:05:02.127
"I said two people would be lonely living here if they weren't good friends.

69
00:05:03.328 --> 00:05:05.389
I think we're good friends now."

70
00:05:05.409 --> 00:05:10.792
"We are pretty good friends," his grandfather admitted.

71
00:05:10.812 --> 00:05:12.413
"Come here."

72
00:05:15.594 --> 00:05:18.516
Cedric scrambled to his side, and the dog followed.

73
00:05:20.128 --> 00:05:22.089
"Is there anything you want?"

74
00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.790
the earl asked.

75
00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:28.313
"Well Cedric began slowly.

76
00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:34.316
"I know we're friends, but I really wish I lived with my mother."

77
00:05:35.717 --> 00:05:36.878
The earl winced.

78
00:05:36.898 --> 00:05:40.440
"You see her almost every day.

79
00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:41.961
Isn't that enough?"

80
00:05:41.981 --> 00:05:47.304
"But I used to see her first thing in the morning and last thing at night.

81
00:05:48.572 --> 00:05:51.493
She was always there, so we had lots of time to talk."

82
00:05:52.993 --> 00:05:55.194
Cedric locked eyes with his grandfather.

83
00:05:56.754 --> 00:05:58.635
Neither said anything for a moment.

84
00:05:59.735 --> 00:06:01.255
Then the earl scowled.

85
00:06:01.275 --> 00:06:04.416
"Do you ever forget about your mother?"

86
00:06:04.436 --> 00:06:09.418
"Never! And she never forgets about me either."

87
00:06:10.378 --> 00:06:12.458
Cedric patted his grandfather's arm.

88
00:06:12.478 --> 00:06:17.760
"Now that I know you, I wouldn't forget about you if we lived apart.

89
00:06:19.152 --> 00:06:21.414
I'd probably think about you even more."

90
00:06:23.576 --> 00:06:24.917
His grandfather nodded.

91
00:06:24.937 --> 00:06:27.319
"I believe you would!"

92
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:34.545
Although the earl had grown fond of Cedric, he couldn't enjoy this warm moment with his grandson.

93
00:06:35.906 --> 00:06:38.108
He was too busy feeling jealous of Mrs.

94
00:06:38.208 --> 00:06:42.392
Errol. But the earl soon had worse problems.
